# The fetched Starkey corpus is a PRIVATE research corpus of another person's
# published work (CCW-B7, "What NOT to do": do not republish or expose it).
# This repository pushes to GitHub, so the captions and metadata stay on disk
# and out of the history. They remain the source of truth locally — everything
# in the `starkey` Postgres schema is rebuilt from them, and nothing here is
# needed to run the app.
#
# Also a size question: ~285 info.json at ~1MB each plus two VTT tracks per
# video is several hundred MB, which does not belong in a source repository.
#
# Charlie: if these should be backed up, R2 is the right home, not git.
meta/
raw/
logs/

# Charlie's transcript documents — same rule as meta/ raw/ logs/ above.
# Untracked is not the same as ignored: without this line the next `git add`
# commits seven full lecture transcripts to a GitHub-backed repo.
*.docx

# Text extracted from those .docx by docx-extract.py — derived from the same
# private transcripts, so it carries the same rule.
_docx_extract/
